Make the Schannel input buffer hold the largest TLS 1.2 record.
The buffer that tls_read and the handshake decrypt from had room for
16384 + 256 bytes, but a TLS 1.2 record may carry up to 16384 + 2048
bytes of ciphertext after its 5-byte header (RFC 5246, 6.2.3), and a
full 16 KiB CBC record with a long MAC and length-hiding padding exceeds
the old size. Such a record could never be completed: the next read
asked for 0 bytes and got 0, which looks like the peer closing the
connection, so the rest of the data was lost (silently, or with a false
"truncated TLS record" now that a close inside a record is reported).
Size the buffer for the maximum.

---
 include/libbb.h |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/libbb.h
+++ b/include/libbb.h
@@ -1018,7 +1018,7 @@
 	CtxtHandle ctx_handle;
 
 	// buffers
-	char in_buffer[16384 + 256]; // input buffer (to read from server), length is maximum TLS packet size
+	char in_buffer[5 + 16384 + 2048]; // input buffer (to read from server), length is maximum TLS packet size
 	unsigned long in_buffer_offset;
 
 	char *out_buffer; // output buffer (for decrypted data, offset from in_buffer)
